==German==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|de|dunckel|tunckel|tunkel||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|tunkel}}, from {{inh|de|goh|tunkal}}, {{m|goh|tuncal||dark}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*dunkalaz||dark}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*dʰengʷ-||to smoke, fume}}. The modern consonantism is [[Central German|Central]] and [[Low German]] (compare {{der|de|gml|dunker}}, also {{m|gml|dunkel}}). Cognate to {{cog|nl|donker||dark}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈdʊŋkəl/|[ˈdʊŋkəl]|[ˈdʊŋkl̩]}}
* {{audio|de|De-at-dunkel.ogg|audio (Austria)}}
* {{audio|de|De-dunkel.ogg|Audio}}

===Adjective===
{{de-adj|stem:-e.comp:+:^[alternatively in Austria].sup:+}}

# {{lb|de|of light, colour}} [[dark]]
#: {{ant|de|hell}}
#: {{ux|de|Im Winter wird es früher '''dunkel'''.|In the winter, it gets '''dark''' earlier.}}
#: {{ux|de|Das '''dunkle''' Rot gefällt mir besser.|I like the '''dark''' red better.}}
# {{lb|de|of sound}} [[deep]]
#: {{syn|de|tief}}
#: {{ant|de|hell|hoch}}
#: {{ux|de|Er hat schon eine ganz '''dunkle''' Stimme.|He’s already got a very '''deep''' voice.}}
# {{lb|de|of memory, ideas}} [[vague]], [[faint]] 
#: {{ux|de|Ich habe nur '''dunkle''' Erinnerungen an meine Großmutter.|I have only '''faint''' memories of my grandmother.}}

